From 5b0d3c2c6be5171b61331efc6c6e8a990b545cac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:48:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Return non-overlapping matches from String.indexes, as
 elm/core does

elm/core's _String_indexes resumes each search at the end of the previous match (i = i + subLen),
so String.indexes "aa" "aaaa" is [0,2]. eco resumed one unit later and returned [0,1,2], so native
programs disagreed with the same program compiled to JavaScript whenever a needle can overlap
itself. The search now resumes after the match on every path, and the header comment no longer
claims that an empty needle gives every index (it gives [], as in elm/core).

StringIndexesTest checks the non-overlapping case and a needle found at UTF-16 unit positions in a
String with a non-ASCII character.
