From 6a2209c2d7fba7c0e116f8ec72a1cc6fdd35b643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:53:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Re-audit the 43 kernel licenses on StringExports.cpp and
 JsArrayExports.cpp

aafc2756 changed both files, so check-kernel-license-manifest.sh stopped the package build. Each
licensed kernel on them gets a re-audit line in kernel-license-audit.csv, and --update re-pins
the two hashes; no license changes.

String.foldl, String.foldr, JsArray.foldl and JsArray.foldr first try Elm::DirectCall, which
calls the step's evaluator directly in the saturated case eco_apply_closure_eval would take, and
falls back to the unchanged helpers otherwise. The callback is still only applied, the
accumulator still flows from one callback result to the next and out, and nothing is stored
